      "message": "std::chrono ugly? How dare you! :)\n\nBut seriously, I\u0027m a fanatical proponent of using C++ APIs in C++ code. Also, std::chrono already showed its superiority in this very change (see the bug in ActivityManager.cpp). At last, std::time_t can\u0027t hold milliseconds and we already have an (ugly) wrapper around clock_gettime in libutils - which I\u0027m migrating from here.",
      "parentUuid": "40326654_bb689baf",
